ed to weigh. Also B's technical competence (computer skills) is good, but we have no explicit technical competence for A, C, D. However A's quick correct decisions may imply technical competence. C has excellent spatial vision, ability to see complex connections, leadership, which suggests technical competence. D solves problems extremely well, concentrates, responsibility.\n\nThus we could argue that A's strengths (reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere) outweigh his communication issues, making him a better fit than B, whose decision quality unknown.\n\nThus we could shift vote to Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention that we previously supported B, but now note that decision quality is a core criterion and we have explicit evidence for A, while B lacks. Also note that A's crew cooperation is actually positive (creates positive atmosphere) despite communication difficulty, whereas B's nasty remarks are more severe.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate A.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\".\n\nNow produce public message."}
